.TH "REPROCTL\-START" "1" "2026" "reproctl" "Repro Development Tools"
.SH NAME
reproctl\-start \- start services via Tilt
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]reproctl start\f[R] \f[I]service\f[R] [\f[I]service\f[R]\&...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Start one or more services from the current context (main checkout or
worktree).
.PP
Service names are validated against the project\(cqs
\f[B]services.json\f[R] manifest.
The requested services are written to \f[B]reproctl_services.json\f[R],
which the Tiltfile reads to determine which resources to enable.
.PP
If the Tilt daemon is not already running, it is started automatically.
.PP
When invoked from a worktree, services are isolated with a
worktree\-slug suffix so they do not conflict with services running from
the main checkout or other worktrees.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
reproctl start api\-server
Start the api\-server from the current context.
.TP
reproctl start api\-server workspace
Start multiple services at once.
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[B]reproctl\f[R](1), \f[B]reproctl\-stop\f[R](1),
\f[B]reproctl\-restart\f[R](1), \f[B]reproctl\-logs\f[R](1)
